<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janiculum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Janiculum is a long hill on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, outside the ancient city's seven hills. In 1849 it was the scene of the fiercest fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a>'s defence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> against the French, and a monument to Garibaldi and memorials to the fallen now stand there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janiculum.jpg" alt="Janiculum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janiculum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
